# Blender interoperability fixture and authoring utilities

Status: DONE
Milestone: M2 interoperability
Dependencies: 13_BLENDER_MODEL_RUNTIME.todo

## Purpose
Use an original technical Blender rig to prove the exported model contract independently
of the future final-art character.

## Tasks
- [x] Build/save/export a canonical rig, weighted meshes, facial keys, texture and clips.
- [x] Supply reusable Blender preflight and export scripts.
- [x] Verify rest pose, weighted deformation, facial mapping, texture orientation and clip sampling.
- [x] Record actual Blender/runtime versions, outputs, hashes and limitations.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Exported files are imported and exercised by the actual runtime.
- [x] No claim of final character art, arbitrary Blender feature support or actual phone qualification.

## Completion evidence
- Blender4.5.14 LTS built/exported both morph-gaze and eye-bone technical fixtures.
- Main export:23mapped bones,964vertices,606triangles,5primitives,1texture,12shape keys,2clips.
- Runtime/Blender vertex errors:2.2469e-7 wave,5.8990e-8 face; eye-gaze movement verified.
- Reusable preflight/export reproduced the GLB SHA256; source .blend was not overwritten.
- examples\blender\conformance-build.json and .local\blender-conformance reports hold exact hashes.

